menu "KTSN LED"

    config KTSN_WIFI
        bool "WiFi station + NTP time sync"
        default y
        help
            Adds the WiFi station and SNTP client (console commands `wifi` and `ntp`).
            The WiFi stack is most of the firmware image (several hundred KB). Without it,
            set the clock with `env time`. Stored WiFi settings are kept either way.

    config KTSN_WIFI_PS_NONE
        bool "Disable WiFi power save"
        depends on KTSN_WIFI
        default y
        help
            Keep the radio fully on (esp_wifi_set_ps(WIFI_PS_NONE)) instead of the IDF default
            WIFI_PS_MIN_MODEM. Uses more power, but on the original ESP32 it removes the LED output
            glitches that WiFi power save causes. Turn off only for battery use where glitches are acceptable.

    config KTSN_SERIAL_API
        bool "Serial JSON API (`api` command, for the IDE)"
        default y
        help
            `api` on the serial console switches it to one JSON request/response per line (responses
            start with 0x1E), sharing the HTTP API's code. Works without WiFi. Adds cJSON (~12 KB) to
            WiFi-less builds. No token: serial access is physical access.

    config KTSN_NET_CLI
        bool "Network CLI (telnet / netcat)"
        depends on KTSN_WIFI
        default y
        help
            The serial console's commands over TCP. Refuses all connections until a token is set
            (`token <secret>`); each session starts with `auth <token>`. Unencrypted: trusted LAN only.

    config KTSN_NET_CLI_PORT
        int "Network CLI TCP port"
        depends on KTSN_NET_CLI
        default 23
        range 1 65535

    config KTSN_HTTP_API
        bool "HTTP/JSON API"
        depends on KTSN_WIFI
        default y
        help
            /api/status, /api/config (GET, PATCH), /api/prog/<n> (PUT), /api/cmd, /api/save, /api/reboot.
            Every request needs "Authorization: Bearer <token>"; with no token set everything is refused.
            Plain HTTP: trusted LAN only. Adds about 60 KB (esp_http_server + cJSON).

    config KTSN_HTTP_PORT
        int "HTTP API TCP port"
        depends on KTSN_HTTP_API
        default 80
        range 1 65534

    config KTSN_MDNS
        bool "mDNS (<hostname>.local) and service discovery"
        depends on KTSN_WIFI
        default y
        help
            Answers as <hostname>.local (default ktsn-led.local, set with `hostname`) and advertises the
            HTTP API (_http._tcp) and network CLI (_telnet._tcp). The hostname is also sent via DHCP.

    config KTSN_OTA
        bool "Firmware updates over the network (POST /api/ota)"
        depends on KTSN_HTTP_API
        default n
        help
            Needs a partition table with two OTA app slots (sdkconfig.flash4mb: partitions_4mb.csv) and is meant
            to be used with CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_APP_ROLLBACK_ENABLE: a new image must come up (render running for
            30 s) or the bootloader goes back to the previous one. Token-protected like the rest of the API; the
            image must be a KTSN LED build for this chip. Not available on 2 MB boards (the image doesn't fit twice).

    choice KTSN_OUTPUT
        prompt "LED output driver"
        default KTSN_OUTPUT_RMT
        help
            How the strings are driven. RMT works on every chip. PARLIO (C6 and other chips with a
            parallel IO peripheral) sends all strings in one DMA transfer, one data line each, so WiFi
            can't disturb the timing and strings are sent in parallel.

        config KTSN_OUTPUT_RMT
            bool "RMT (led_strip), one RMT channel per string"

        config KTSN_OUTPUT_PARLIO
            bool "PARLIO, all strings in one parallel DMA transfer"
            depends on SOC_PARLIO_SUPPORTED
            help
                Up to 8 strings, any GPIOs. One frame is sent at once and must fit in 65535 bytes:
                15 bytes per pixel of the longest string, times the lane count rounded up to 1/2/4/8
                (2 strings: up to 2184 px each). Bit timing equals led_strip's WS2812 RMT timing.
    endchoice

    config KTSN_RMT_MEM_SYMBOLS
        int "RMT memory per LED channel (symbols, 0 = driver default)"
        depends on KTSN_OUTPUT_RMT
        default 256 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32 && KTSN_WIFI
        default 64 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32
        default 96 if (IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6) && KTSN_WIFI
        default 0
        range 0 512
        help
            RMT symbols (one per data bit) buffered per LED channel. Without RMT DMA (ESP32, C3, C6;
            only S3/P4 have it) the driver refills this buffer from an interrupt in halves while a frame
            is sent; more memory means fewer refills and more slack, so WiFi interrupt latency causes
            fewer glitches. Use a multiple of the chip's block size; channels that don't fit fail at
            boot with a log message and stay dark.
            ESP32: 64-symbol blocks, 512 total (64: 8 ch, 128: 4, 256: 2, 512: 1). Default 256 with WiFi
            (verified glitch-free), 64 without.
            C3/C6: 48-symbol blocks, 2 TX channels. Default 96 with WiFi (1 channel), untested; these
            chips are single-core, so WiFi and LED output share the CPU.

endmenu
